# {{ .inputs.repo_name }}

{{ if .inputs.description }}{{ .inputs.description }}{{ else }}A Substrate app.{{ end }}

Built on [Substrate](https://github.com/hollis-labs/substrate): the manifest (`cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/substrate.yaml`)
selects the modules, `substrate generate` writes `substrate_wiring.go`, and `internal/` is the app.

## First build

```sh
go mod tidy
go run github.com/hollis-labs/substrate/cmd/substrate pins sync --app .
go mod tidy
go run github.com/hollis-labs/substrate/cmd/substrate validate -f cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}/substrate.yaml
go build ./cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}
```

## Run

The owner is created offline, never over HTTP (see `docs/identity-bootstrap.md`):

```sh
printf '%s\n' "$OWNER_PASSWORD" | ./{{ .inputs.repo_name }} identity setup --username owner
./{{ .inputs.repo_name }} serve
```

Settings are keys in the YAML file named by `SUBSTRATE_CONFIG` (for example `httphost.addr`); the only
environment variable the app reads is `{{ upper (replace "-" "_" .inputs.repo_name) }}_DATA_DIR`.

## UI

`frontend/` is a React app on app-shell and the BOM-pinned kits. **First step: `cd frontend && npm install`,
then commit `package-lock.json`** (CI runs `npm ci` and fails without the lock). Then `make ui-build` builds into `internal/webui/dist`, which the binary
embeds; `make ui-dev` runs the dev server (port 5173) against a running backend.

**Signing in through the dev server.** The dev server proxies `/api` without changing the `Origin`, and
identity refuses a cookie write from an origin that is not the backend's own (`403 bad_origin`). In your
**development** override file (the one `SUBSTRATE_CONFIG` names on your machine), and only there, add:

```yaml
identity:
  allowed_origins: ["http://127.0.0.1:5173"]
```

Never put `allowed_origins` in `substrate.yaml` or in a deployed config.

## Checks

`go vet ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, `golangci-lint run`, `substrate pins check --app .` and
`substrate scan-public --ref HEAD` (CI runs all of them).
